Shared tooling for the G23 reproducers (WORK=.../work/G23-vdgraph-dorder)
  dtest.c    PT-Scotch driver: dtest <graph> <base|-1> order|map|part <strategy|""> <nparts> <save> <outfile|->
             save: o/t/m/b = dgraphOrderSave/SaveTree/SaveMap/SaveBlock, s = dgraphMapSave (MapInit without user part array, as dgmap), n = none.
             Linked with libptscotcherr (non-exiting errorPrint); uses MPI_Init_thread(MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE) because fold-dup
             coarsening runs MPI-communicating threads (with plain MPI_Init, as in the first pass's drv.c, strategies that fold hang at random).
             Build: mpicc -g -O0 -fsanitize=address,undefined -I$B/include dtest.c -o dtest_<tree> -L$B/lib -lptscotch -lscotch -lptscotcherr -lz -lm -lrt -pthread -ldl
             (use -fsanitize=undefined only for the LD_PRELOAD trees buildfi/buildfip). Arms the fault injector (fi_armed) around the compute call.
  dmaptest.c internal-API driver for dmapSave (see DMO-15/README).
  fishim.c   G18's LD_PRELOAD malloc injector + FI_FUNC=<routine substring>: only allocations whose backtrace contains the routine are counted.
             gcc -O1 -g -fPIC -shared -o fishim.so fishim.c -ldl ; SIGUSR1 prints a backtrace of a hung rank.
  scan.sh    G18's scanner: scan.sh LIBDIR BIN NP FAILRANK FROM TO -- args  (exports FI_FUNC; HANG = 15 s timeout).
  Trees: build = series (32-bit ASan+UBSan), buildp = base-combined copy (same flags), build64 = series 64-bit, buildfi/buildfip = base/series
         with -fsanitize=undefined only, builddbg = series with -DSCOTCH_DEBUG_ALL. "pristine" below means base-combined (== v7.0.17 for these files).
  Data: 4elt.grf (base 0, 15606 vertices), lbl.grf (12-vertex path, base 1, labels 101..112), lbl13/lbl14.grf (same, 13/14 vertices),
        st_z.txt / st_df.txt (first pass's strategies: low=z / d{} inside band graphs), st_df_nofold.txt.
  Logs kept here: scan_df_pristine.txt, scan_df_patched.txt, redo.txt (G20 guard hang test + scans), dmo12proof.txt, trace.* (hang traces).
